# P14 D4 — what the daemon is allowed to see.
#
# There was no `.dockerignore` until the first real image build: compose's context is the repository root, so every
# build tarred `.git` (40 MB of history), `web/node_modules` (577 MB) and `web/.next` (78 MB) and shipped them to
# the daemon before the first instruction ran. Neither Dockerfile copies any of it — the copies are explicit
# (`packages`, `services/api`, `db`, `brand`, `tools` and `requirements.txt`) — so this changes no image, it stops
# the build from carrying the workspace.
#
# The rule for entries here: exclude only what no `COPY` needs. `tools/` and `brand/` are copied by the API image;
# the web tree and the git history are not copied by anything, and `.git` additionally carries every secret that
# was ever committed before it was rotated.
.git
.gitignore
.dockerignore

# Dependencies and build output: never inside an image, all of it rebuildable.
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/dist
**/build
**/coverage
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache

# The agent/skill scaffolding and local tool caches: workspace furniture, not product.
.agents
skills
.arena
.cache
.local
plans

# Anything an operator keeps beside the code but never inside an artefact.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/.secrets
**/*.pem
**/*.key
